WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.709
RUFUS: Access and confidence are,
again, different documents.

00:00:03.922 --> 00:00:06.233
JAMIE: He's going to put that on a
mug.

00:00:06.298 --> 00:00:07.779
RUFUS: I've earned it today.

00:00:07.992 --> 00:00:11.925
ALEX: But here's what I find
genuinely interesting —

00:00:11.925 --> 00:00:15.858
ALEX: Google choosing Oracle
specifically. Oracle has
enterprise credibility

00:00:15.858 --> 00:00:19.792
ALEX: in industries where Google
Cloud historically hasn't.
Finance,

00:00:19.792 --> 00:00:23.725
ALEX: healthcare-adjacent
workloads, government-adjacent
procurement.

00:00:23.835 --> 00:00:26.758
RUFUS: That's the non-obvious part
of the channel strategy.

00:00:26.758 --> 00:00:29.680
RUFUS: It's not just distribution.
It's credibility transfer.
Oracle's

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:32.602
RUFUS: existing relationships
carry Google's chips into rooms
where

00:00:32.602 --> 00:00:35.525
RUFUS: Google wouldn't have been
the first call.

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:38.607
JAMIE: Which means TPU adoption
might happen sideways —

00:00:38.607 --> 00:00:41.580
JAMIE: not because a developer
chose them, but because

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:44.552
JAMIE: a procurement team already
trusted Oracle.
